==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows audit entries to have non-Read access types (e.g., Write, Delete). This directly violates the append-only invariant and v1's read-only scope. The assertions should fail when this structural constraint is removed.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutability, FR_005_ReadOnlyScope
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutability: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_ReadOnlyScope: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccessRule  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccessRule.als
    rationale: Removing this fact permits authorized access without requiring care-team membership. The model can then have Permitted outcomes where no active CareTeamMembership exists, violating the core authorization rule.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamAuthorizationEnforced
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CareTeamAuthorizationEnforced: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakage  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakage.als
    rationale: Removing this fact decouples outcome types from their authorisation basis. The model can then have Denied outcomes with PatientNotFound basis or vice versa, which leaks information about whether a patient exists.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentResponses
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentResponses: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact permits audit entries with recorded clinician fields that don't match any real clinician in the system. This violates the integrity of the audit trail and allows misattribution.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_009_AuditEntryShape
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_AuditEntryShape: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NonEmptyUniverse  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_NonEmptyUniverse.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to have an empty universe with no clinicians, patients, or audit entries. This makes quantified assertions vacuously true (e.g., 'all ae: AuditEntry | ...' is trivially true when no audit entries exist), masking the actual invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: This is the most direct structural constraint on immutability. Removing it is the primary way to test that the AppendOnly assertion genuinely constrains the model.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

